# {{ project_name }}

A kandra-generated SDK for **{{ display_name }}**.{# TODO: link kandra to its repo when public #}

## Quick start

```bash
poetry install
poetry run kandra validate kandra.yaml   # sanity-check the manifest
poetry run kandra build kandra.yaml      # generate the client SDK into dist/
poetry run pytest                        # run the smoke test
```

## What's in here

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `kandra.yaml` | The manifest — single source of truth for transports, commands, etc. |
| `src/{{ package_name }}/handlers/` | One Python class per command. Edit these to add device logic. |
| `src/{{ package_name }}/codecs/` | Encoder/decoder for on-the-wire payloads. |
| `src/{{ package_name }}/transports/` | Thin adapter wrappers around `kandra-runtime` transports. |
| `examples/connect.py` | Tiny example showing how to construct + call the generated client. |
| `tests/test_smoke.py` | Validates the manifest on every test run. |

